#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083004 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083203 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c47216a0-3e51-50bb-b7eb-f92592db5dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial Using Synthetic Division"}] :question/id #uuid "551cceca-a69f-57c1-b4b0-c8f7aedd3cdc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5146" :question/problem "Use synthetic division to divide $5x^4+x^3+6x+2$ by $x+1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing an $x^2$ term, so we insert a $0x^2$ in its place and carry out the process in the same way.\n\n![](images/46/469e53d0e8ca69548d5385e8a4f75c3c366c59ce0c48b7eccf71f6bdb5577fcc.svg)\n\nSince the remainder is $0,$ it means that $x+1$ divides $5x^4+x^3+6x+2$ exactly and gives a quotient of $5x^3-4x^2+4x+2.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x^4+x^3+6x+2}{x+1} = 5x^3-4x^2+4x+2 .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083005 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083204 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b0a87cd-e9b5-5ca1-8132-b62a715264ac" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial With Leading Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "6d179766-30a7-5cd9-ba38-2ee6f49d37b8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5149" :question/problem "Find the quotient and remainder of $\\dfrac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{2-3x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the divisor in standard form as $-3x+2.$ Then, we factor out the leading coefficient. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-10x+8}{-3x+2} & =\\frac{3{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-10x+8}{-3(x-\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{3{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-10x+8}{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process on $\\dfrac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)},$ remembering to include a coefficient of zero for the $x^2$ term, we arrive at the following:\n\n![](images/7a/7a44598088833fa475191b39579bb82935074ae5c470e5a2139555818b91af08.svg)\n\nReading off the bottom row, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x^4+7x^3-10x+8}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)} = 3x^3+9x^2+6x-6+\\frac{4}{\\left(x-\\frac23\\right)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply by the original $-\\dfrac 1 3$ factor to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{4}+7{x}^{3}-10x+8}{2-3x} & =-\\frac{1}{3}(3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+6x-6+\\frac{4}{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-2x+2+\\frac{4}{2-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083204 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b0a87cd-e9b5-5ca1-8132-b62a715264ac" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial With Leading Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28481e03-c1c4-5f3e-83d7-ab1fbae85a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520851} {:answer/id #uuid "53c86c1b-3036-55c5-85ff-2b7cf6a4cd21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520954} {:answer/id #uuid "77fb4b5e-897c-5ba2-93cd-e5ced7af3f1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521032} {:answer/id #uuid "b9080672-7e99-5db6-a47d-8bd2cd68cf73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521175} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b31f76-5489-52c8-bea0-fceb9cc6bd92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-2-\\frac{3}{2x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28481e03-c1c4-5f3e-83d7-ab1fbae85a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520851} :answer-field/id #uuid "31effb53-6d38-5d2b-a024-6dd5298f9ade" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74edae7f-921c-52ab-b265-0f5c05fcd5a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-18648" :question/problem "$\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2x+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate $\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2x+1}$ using synthetic division.\n\nFor synthetic division to work, we need the coefficient of $x$ in the denominator to be equal to $1.$ So first, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2x+1} & =\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process on $\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}$, we arrive at the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 8 & 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & -4 & 0 & 1 \\\\  & 8 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})} & =\\frac{1}{2}(8{x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x-1}{2x+1}=4{x}^{2}-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083204 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b0a87cd-e9b5-5ca1-8132-b62a715264ac" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial With Leading Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019b887d-bf4a-554b-963c-0cfc346b873b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-1+\\frac{5}{6x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520766} {:answer/id #uuid "142e1cea-140f-5872-936a-5a1bb03e406e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-\\frac{5}{6x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520811} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc3a8d8-690d-59bb-86ec-c9b3a4aaa664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+2+\\frac{5}{6x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521044} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a06afe-f8a5-5241-8ff2-96045c897fa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+1+\\frac{5}{6x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521171} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cf598d-2125-51cc-895b-f9c3da066eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5+\\frac{5}{6x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9cf598d-2125-51cc-895b-f9c3da066eb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5+\\frac{5}{6x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521311} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ea95026-8e39-5cf6-afd5-80e17b2a0504" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2b65857-f961-5afd-9ef2-0421d5a69f7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-19186" :question/problem "$\\frac{18{x}^{2}+27x}{6x-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate $\\frac{18{x}^{2}+27x}{6x-1}$ using synthetic division.\n\nFor synthetic division to work, we need the coefficient of $x$ in the denominator to be equal to $1.$ So first, we factor the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{18{x}^{2}+27x}{6x-1} & =\\frac{18{x}^{2}+27x}{6(x-\\frac{1}{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{18{x}^{2}+27x}{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process on $\\frac{18{x}^{2}+27x}{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}$, we arrive at the following:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $18$ | $27$ | $0$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n|  | $18$ | $30$ | $5$ |\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{18{x}^{2}+27x}{(x-\\frac{1}{6})} & =\\frac{1}{6}(18x+30+\\frac{5}{(x-\\frac{1}{6})}) \\\\  & =3x+5+\\frac{5}{6x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{18{x}^{2}+27x}{6x-1}=3x+5+\\frac{5}{6x-1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083203 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c47216a0-3e51-50bb-b7eb-f92592db5dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial Using Synthetic Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76ba2d94-4d0f-5625-b4fa-7c143eff88d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+31x+109+\\frac{546}{x-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521027} {:answer/id #uuid "a35b14bc-ccb3-5c93-b237-5c5f1e489e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+22x+109+\\frac{546}{x-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521132} {:answer/id #uuid "ad57b36e-4935-5ec1-a05f-5c4149783a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-18x-87+\\frac{316}{x-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521150} {:answer/id #uuid "c7caa57e-8215-5335-a5e5-24c26f1cc179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+22x+126+\\frac{546}{x-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521208} {:answer/id #uuid "fc85e694-f575-5c45-afd7-78e57139337f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+22x+148+\\frac{356}{x-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a35b14bc-ccb3-5c93-b237-5c5f1e489e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+22x+109+\\frac{546}{x-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521132} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c1b8643-2073-5117-9e8e-454f21b95ef8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de8f069f-9a0c-5798-9f23-be0540a99a8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-5902" :question/problem "$\\frac{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x+1}{x-5}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate $\\frac{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x+1}{x-5}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $4$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $20$ | $110$ | $545$ |\n|  | $4$ | $22$ | $109$ | $546$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x+1}{x-5}=4{x}^{2}+22x+109+\\frac{546}{x-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083203 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c47216a0-3e51-50bb-b7eb-f92592db5dbc" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial Using Synthetic Division"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000f20c9-eed8-54f6-abc2-91ab1c18f546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+5+\\frac{5}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520764} {:answer/id #uuid "3187e3c7-0514-556c-842f-9facdb881681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+6+\\frac{5}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520869} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1ad295-850f-513c-968f-e870eb960421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520932} {:answer/id #uuid "a089de6a-9ae9-59ae-bc4b-65be3819ab12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+1+\\frac{5}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521123} {:answer/id #uuid "f94cbbcb-f375-5b97-b880-c565c568eb32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-6-\\frac{5}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a1ad295-850f-513c-968f-e870eb960421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520932} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b57361f-00f1-5ff6-8cda-424c1fb2e5d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4aae2ef4-175a-54ac-96cd-b00f03406c30" :question/math-academy-id "q-7670" :question/problem "$\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate $\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}=2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
